 of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the inked margin of the specimen along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  A stain for E cadherin shows lack of membranous staining of the tumor cells  confirming the diagnoses of invasive lobular carcinoma and lobular neoplasia  lobular carcinoma in situ   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of breast tissue  oriented as follows  Short stitch anterior  long stitch lateral  bow tie cephalad  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm firm  irregular  tan white mass that abuts the posterior margin  and comes to 1 1cm of the superior margin  1 3cm of the anterior margin  2 0cm from the inferior margin  1 5cm from the medial margin and 1 5cm from the lateral margin  The mass is encircled by dense white rubbery fibrotic tissue  The remainder of the breast contains focal rubbery fibrotic areas admixed with fat  the latter of which predominate  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest margins  superior and posterior    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of more fibrotic appearing area adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrosis away from mass  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm unoriented portion of breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ellipse of tan skin on one surface  Also received in the same container are two irregular fragments of detached fatty tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The specimen is inked entirely in black  and serially sectioned to reveal diffusely dense tan white to tan yellow rubbery tissue  with focal areas of adipose tissue  located predominantly in the deepest aspect of the specimen  REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm from the skin surface  No focally distinct firmer areas are appreciated  The denser areas abut the inked margin  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   Se